<h1>Tools</h1>
<p>Interactive tools beyond the generated reference pages this wiki already has -- some built, some still planned.</p>

<h2 id="trades-price-guide">Trades price guide</h2>
<p>
  Every individual buy/sell listing across every wandering trader specialization, flattened into
  one sortable, filterable table (price/stock shown as a range, not just an average) -- in the
  spirit of <a href="https://www.vintagestorypriceguide.com/">vintagestorypriceguide.com</a>.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}trades/">Open the trades page &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="schematic-vieweruploader">Schematic viewer</h2>
<p>
  Upload a <code>.json</code> schematic (or open a bundled sample) and inspect it in 3D: block
  legend with show/hide, a floor-by-floor slider, and click-to-inspect with decoded block-entity
  data. Merged in from
  <a href="https://github.com/jgwoolley/vintage-story-schematic-preview">jgwoolley/vintage-story-schematic-preview</a>.
  Every worldgen schematic in the game and its mods can be opened directly from its
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}schematics/">schematic page</a> or from a structure page.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/schematic/">Open the schematic viewer &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="waypoint-planner">WayPoint planner</h2>
<p>
  Track waypoints and translocator links on a map and find the cheapest route between any two.
  Ported from the vintage-story-price-guide project.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/waypoints/">Open the WayPoint planner &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="calendar">Calendar</h2>
<p>
  Convert an in-game date into elapsed game days and real-life hours.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/calendar/">Open the calendar &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="paintingtapestry-in-ruins-lookup">Painting/tapestry-in-ruins lookup</h2>
<p class="wip-badge">Work in progress</p>
<p>
  Right now, each <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}paintings/">painting</a>/
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tapestries/">tapestry</a> page (and now, generally, every
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}items/">item/block</a> page) shows which
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}structures/">structures</a> it's found in, built from a
  flat pass over every schematic's block-code dictionary -- confirms the code is somewhere in that
  schematic, not where or how many times. Tapestries already get a precise, per-instance version
  of this (see the <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tapestries/">tapestries page</a>, decoded
  directly from each schematic's block-entity data); a proper lookup for paintings would need the
  same per-instance decoding, evaluated against <code>worldgen/storystructures.json</code> and
  <code>worldgen/structures.json</code> directly.
</p>

<h2 id="chiseled-block-viewer">Chiseled blocks</h2>
<p>
  The <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/schematic/">schematic viewer</a> decodes chiseled blocks:
  click one and the block panel lists the materials it is made from, draws its shape in 3D and can export it as a
  file for QPTech's ChiselTools mod, with instructions on where to put it. (The main 3D view still draws a chiseled
  block as a plain cube.) See the <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}research/">research page</a> for the data format.
</p>

<h2 id="chiseled-shape-viewer">Chiseled shape viewer</h2>
<p>
  Upload a shape file saved by QPTech's ChiselTools mod (<code>.pf save</code>) and see the chiseled block in 3D with its
  materials, or find the same shape in the game's schematics.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/chisel-shape/">Open the chiseled shape viewer &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="schematic-block-item-search">Schematic block/item search</h2>
<p>
  Search every worldgen schematic for a block or item: where it is placed, which chiseled blocks use it as a
  material, which containers hold it and which random placeholders could produce it. The files are fetched and
  decoded in your browser, nothing is precomputed. Every item page links here with its code filled in.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/schematic-search/">Open the schematic search &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="alloy-ratio-calculator">Alloy ratio calculator</h2>
<p>
  A slider per metal in an alloy (each limited to the recipe's allowed range) that computes the
  most metal bits a 4-slot crucible can hold at that ratio, using the real bit stack sizes.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/alloy/">Open the alloy calculator &rarr;</a>
</p>

<h2 id="seed-climate-lookup">Seed climate lookup</h2>
<p>
  Enter a numeric world seed, the climate world options and a position to get the generated
  temperature, rainfall and geologic activity there, plus which wild plants and trees from this
  wiki's data can grow in that climate. A browser port of the game's realistic climate generator
  (seeded per-cell randomness + the north&ndash;south temperature gradient), approximate because the
  game's final simplex "wobble", forest/shrub maps and terrain height aren't ported.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tools/climate/">Open the seed climate lookup &rarr;</a>
</p>
